Falsifies `grant_plan::word::verification::a_word_is_a_slice_of_its_token_and_quoted_only_when_wrapped`.

The defect: a quote that closes before the end of the token is taken as wrapping all of it, so `'a'b` reads as the quoted word `a'`.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(!w.text.contains(&quote))`, or its check that a quoted word ends in its quote.

diff --git a/src/word.rs b/src/word.rs
--- a/src/word.rs
+++ b/src/word.rs
@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@
     let inner = &token[1..];
     match inner.iter().position(|&b| b == first) {
         // The closing quote is the last byte, so the pair wraps the whole token.
-        Some(at) if at + 2 == token.len() => Ok(Word {
+        Some(at) if at + 2 <= token.len() => Ok(Word {
             text: &token[1..token.len() - 1],
             quoted: true,
         }),
